    {
      "id": "claim_68cd767133cf4d50a0a4520cad182cc7",
      "statement": "The agent sandbox is the only guard at execution time: a `LocalShellExecutor` confined to the worktree with a scrubbed environment, a ten-minute command timeout, and a deny-list of destructive/network/git-publishing patterns, run with approvals disabled and execute mode — which also means a hostile issue body cannot read credentials from the agent's shell environment, the code-level answer to the PRD's prompt-injection risk.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/Agent/Roles/ImplementationAgent.cs#L21-L72",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:85acf3228527072ecf2fae90b01191ec0e6b868744d725091ce4723b7a27e2ca:"
