    {
      "id": "claim_f9a51271cd904878af2270ffd0577ce9",
      "statement": "Today the code implements exactly one intake gate and one terminal stage: an open issue labeled `feature` passes the seven-section spec check and is then either commented on and closed as `not_planned`, or — only if it also carries `ready-for-agent` — handed to `JobQueue.TryAdd` as an `ImplementSpec` job that prepares a worktree, runs the agent, and ends with a completion log. All other PRD §3.1 stages (bug validation, `needs-triage`, label transitions, commit/push, PR, review/`merge` commands, cost caps) have no code.",
      "evidence": [
