    {
      "id": "claim_7a02af81281240ceb80cc9ff21881885",
      "statement": "The code enforces several behaviors the PRD never describes, so the PRD under-documents the design: a third state constant `ready-for-agent` acting as the only approval/start gate, a hard `owner`/`repository`-versus-`origin` identity check that throws inside `PrepareWorkspaceAsync`, a process-wide `static SemaphoreSlim PrepareLock` serializing all fetch/fast-forward/worktree work, a `PushEvent` handler that logs the ref then runs `git fetch`/ff-only sync inline inside the HTTP request for `refs/heads/main` only, and a seven-section spec contract shared with `skills/to-spec/SKILL.md` by a comment rather than by a test.",
