    {
      "id": "claim_466cdc387c2244ffb1978ad5d886b12d",
      "statement": "The only mitigation of the PRD's 'never write security details to public channels' rule is architectural rather than a control: the agent has no GitHub tool and never posts, so the single outbound text the system can emit is the fixed English `Closed: the spec is missing required sections: …` comment — which also means the PRD's §5 #6 rule that comments follow the issue's language is unimplemented.",
