    {
      "id": "claim_21bd21eb500047c0a357d8be59edc60a",
      "statement": "The agent authority boundary is layered in a way the PRD does not state: git and GitHub are forbidden in both the role `Instructions` and the per-run prompt, while the shell deny-list blocks only a subset (`git push|reset|clean|checkout --`, `gh`, network fetchers), leaving `git commit`/`git add` prompt-enforced, and file tools are rooted at the worktree with all approvals disabled, meaning writes are permitted rather than restricted.",
